From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:22:35 +0300
Subject: Sockets non-blocking on big-endian 64-bit too (FIONBIO takes an int)

net_set_non_blocking() and net_set_blocking() gave ioctl(FIONBIO) a pointer to an unsigned
long. Linux reads an int there (sock_ioctl: get_user on an int *). On little-endian the int is
the long's low half and holds the 1; on big-endian 64-bit (ppc64, s390x) it is the high half,
0, so the UDP sockets of the client and the server stayed blocking.

What that did on the PS3 (Debian ppc64, 0.7.5-3), and the same under qemu-ppc64 user mode:
the client connects to a local teeworlds-server, gets the token and the accept ("got accept.
connection online"), then sits in recvfrom() inside CNetClient::Recv (PumpNetwork's loop)
waiting for a packet that never comes: the server waits for the client's NETMSG_INFO, which
the client sends only on its next main loop pass. No frame after that, the screen stays on
the last loading frame (52%). A blocking server also ticks only when a packet arrives.

Windows keeps the unsigned long (ioctlsocket takes a u_long *).

diff --git a/src/base/system.c b/src/base/system.c
--- a/src/base/system.c
+++ b/src/base/system.c
@@ -1279,13 +1279,17 @@ NETSOCKET net_tcp_create(NETADDR bindaddr)
 
 int net_set_non_blocking(NETSOCKET sock)
 {
+#if defined(CONF_FAMILY_WINDOWS)
 	unsigned long mode = 1;
+#else
+	int mode = 1; /* FIONBIO takes an int on Linux: an unsigned long read as an int is 0 on big-endian 64-bit */
+#endif
 	if(sock.ipv4sock >= 0)
 	{
 #if defined(CONF_FAMILY_WINDOWS)
 		ioctlsocket(sock.ipv4sock, FIONBIO, (unsigned long *)&mode);
 #else
-		ioctl(sock.ipv4sock, FIONBIO, (unsigned long *)&mode);
+		ioctl(sock.ipv4sock, FIONBIO, &mode);
 #endif
 	}
 
@@ -1294,7 +1298,7 @@ int net_set_non_blocking(NETSOCKET sock)
 #if defined(CONF_FAMILY_WINDOWS)
 		ioctlsocket(sock.ipv6sock, FIONBIO, (unsigned long *)&mode);
 #else
-		ioctl(sock.ipv6sock, FIONBIO, (unsigned long *)&mode);
+		ioctl(sock.ipv6sock, FIONBIO, &mode);
 #endif
 	}
 
@@ -1303,13 +1307,17 @@ int net_set_non_blocking(NETSOCKET sock)
 
 int net_set_blocking(NETSOCKET sock)
 {
+#if defined(CONF_FAMILY_WINDOWS)
 	unsigned long mode = 0;
+#else
+	int mode = 0; /* FIONBIO takes an int on Linux: an unsigned long read as an int is 0 on big-endian 64-bit */
+#endif
 	if(sock.ipv4sock >= 0)
 	{
 #if defined(CONF_FAMILY_WINDOWS)
 		ioctlsocket(sock.ipv4sock, FIONBIO, (unsigned long *)&mode);
 #else
-		ioctl(sock.ipv4sock, FIONBIO, (unsigned long *)&mode);
+		ioctl(sock.ipv4sock, FIONBIO, &mode);
 #endif
 	}
 
@@ -1318,7 +1326,7 @@ int net_set_blocking(NETSOCKET sock)
 #if defined(CONF_FAMILY_WINDOWS)
 		ioctlsocket(sock.ipv6sock, FIONBIO, (unsigned long *)&mode);
 #else
-		ioctl(sock.ipv6sock, FIONBIO, (unsigned long *)&mode);
+		ioctl(sock.ipv6sock, FIONBIO, &mode);
 #endif
 	}
 
